(4) In the performance of his functions under this Act the patron shall act and bebound in tlte same manner as the Governor of a Provlnce acrs and is bound under Article 105of the constitution of the Isramic Repubric of pakistan.9' rnspection an inquiry.- (1) The Patron may direct inspection or inquiry into theaffairs of the Institute.(2) The Patron shall convey his views with regard to the result of the inspection orinquiry to the Board and may, after ascertaining the ,i'"*, of the Board, recommend anyremedial action to the Board.(3) The Board shall, within the time.specified by the Patron, submit a report to thePatron about the action taken on the recommendaiions of the patron.(4) If the Board fails to take action to the satisfaction of the patron within thespecified time, the Patron may issue such directions as he thinks fit and ttre goarJshail complywith the direction.(5) The Patron may, on the recommendation of a commiffee constituted by him andcomprising a nominee of the Board, a nominee of the Higher Education Department of theGovernment, not below the rank of an Additional secreta ryZiaa professor or vice chancellorof any public sector university, take action against the Inst-itute by appointing an administrator,who shall exercise the powers of the Board to run the affairs of the Institute till such time asmay be specified by the patron.(6) The Patron shall not take any action under subsection (5), unless the Chairmanis afforded an opportunity of hearing.(7) The Patron may set aside a decision or action ofthe Board, which, in the opinionof th-e patron, is against the obiectives of the Institute or against the interest of academicexcellence, religious or cultural ideology or national integrity.10'- Rector'- (l) The Patron shall, on the recommendations of the Board, appoint a personas Rector for a term of four years on such terms and conditions as may be determined by theBoard.@ The Board shall recommend a person for appointment as Rector from amongstthe panel of three persons recommended by thl Search c#mitt"".(3) The Rector shall be the person who possesses the prescribed qualifications andexperience.(4) The Rector shall perform such functions as are given in this Act or as may beprescribed or as are assigned to him by the Board.1I' owers of the-Rector.-(l) The Rector shall be the Chief Executive Officer of theInstitute responsible for all administrative antl academic functions of the Institute and forensuring that the provisions of this Act, rules, statutes nnd rcg ;lations are observed in all affairsof the institute.@ The Rector may attend a meeting of an Authority or body of the Institute.(3) subject to the cqnditions u! -uy be prescribed 6y the Btard, the Rector may,in case of an emergency, take an action which is not othenvise in the competence ofthe Rectorand within three days of taking of such action, shall submit a report of the action taken to theChairperson of the Board.(4) Subject to the general supervision and control of the Board, the Rector may:(a) direct a teacher, officer or. other employee of the lnstitute to take upsuch assignment in connection with eiamination, administration or anyother activities in the Institute as hg may considei necessary;
