(c) two experts to be appointed by the Dean of the Facurty.(2) The term of office of members of the Board of studies, other than ex-officiomembers, shall be three years.(3) The quorum for meetings of the Board of studies shall be one-half of thenumber of members, a fraction being counted as one.7. unctions of the Board of Studies.- (l) The Board of studies shail:(a) propose to the Academic council through the concerned Board ofFaculty cu*icula and syilabi for ail degrle, aipr..u-*a certificatecourses in the subject or subjects concernid;(b) recommend the names of paper-settlrs and examiners in the subject orsubjects concerned; and(c) perform such other firnctions as may be prescribed by the Regulationsand the Rules from time to time.(2) The Rector may make, repeal or amend Rules pertaining to the establishmentand operation of the Boards ofstudie;.8' selection Board.- (r) The Serection Board shail consist of;(a) Rector (Convener);(b) the Dean of the Faculty concerned;(c) the Head of Department concerned;(d) one member of the Board to be nominated by theBoard;(e) one eminent schorar to be nominated by the Foundation;(0 one expert in the subject to be norninated by the Secretary to theGovernment, Higher Education Department;(g) the Registrar, who shall be the Secretary of the Selection Board; and(h) a representative of Higher Educatiori bepartment, not below the rankof Deputy Secretary.tt r"" y.l2lr. The members other than ex-fficro members shall hold office for a period of. of the #]"r,", l""Xlilembers of the selection Board shall constitute the quorum for a meeting(4) No member who is a candidate or whose familymember is a candidate, for a post to which appoi tment is to be made, shalr take part inthe proceedings of the selection Board for sellction of a candica-te on such post.(5) In selection of candidates for the post of P;;ferro. o, Associate plofessor, theSelection Board shall co-opt or consult three experts in the subject concerned "J il selectingcandidates for any other teaching post, t ro .*pirt. i, irr" rro:;ct concerned, to be nominatedby the Rector from a.standing.list of experts for each subject approved by the Board on therecommendations ofthe SelectionBoard. -J---(6) The Board may revise the standing list of experts of a subject on therecommendations of the Selection Board.9. unctions of the serection Board.- The Serection Board shail:(a) consider the applications and recommend to the Board, the names of suitablecandidates for appointrnent to teaching and other posts; and(b) consider all.caies of promotion or silection or officers of the Institute andreconrmend the names of suitable candidates for such promotion or selectionto the Board. ,
